# Routing rules (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_redirects` format).
#
# WHY THERE IS NO `/*  /index.html  200` CATCH-ALL
# ------------------------------------------------
# The usual SPA rule rewrites every unmatched URL to the app shell with a 200.
# That makes it impossible for the site to ever return a real 404: mistyped and
# dead URLs answer "200 OK" with a page that says "not found", which is a soft
# 404. Google treats those as a crawl-budget drain and may index them.
#
# Because `npm run build` prerenders every known route to its own HTML file,
# real pages resolve as static files and need no rewrite. Anything genuinely
# unknown falls through to 404.html, which the host serves with a true HTTP 404
# status.
#
# The rules below are the exceptions: routes that are real but cannot be
# prerendered because their content is dynamic or private.

# Blog articles come from Supabase, so their slugs aren't known at build time.
/blog/*                 /index.html   200

# Authenticated / non-indexed app routes.
/admin                  /index.html   200
/admin/*                /index.html   200
/auth                   /index.html   200
/auth/*                 /index.html   200
/whatsapp-sent          /index.html   200
/privacy-dashboard      /index.html   200
/privacy-dashboard/*    /index.html   200

# Everything else: no rule. Unknown paths -> 404.html with HTTP 404.
